{
  "id": "21208_sacchi",
  "headword": "{察知|さっち}",
  "reading": "さっち",
  "romaji": "sacchi",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "sensing; perceiving; detecting",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "sensing; perceiving; detecting",
      "explanation": "The act of becoming aware of something through intuition or keen observation, often before it becomes obvious. Implies picking up on subtle cues rather than being told directly."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "21208_sacchi_ex1",
      "japanese": "{危険|きけん}を{察知|さっち}する。",
      "english": "To sense danger.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "21208_sacchi_ex2",
      "japanese": "{動物|どうぶつ}は{地震|じしん}を{事前|じぜん}に{察知|さっち}すると{言|い}われている。",
      "english": "Animals are said to sense earthquakes in advance.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "21208_sacchi_ex3",
      "japanese": "{彼女|かのじょ}の{表情|ひょうじょう}から{何|なに}か{問題|もんだい}があることを{察知|さっち}した。",
      "english": "I sensed from her expression that something was wrong.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "A する verb ({察知|さっち}する). Composed of {察|さつ} (guess, sense) + {知|ち} (know). Implies becoming aware of something through intuition, subtle observation, or instinct rather than through direct information.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {危険|きけん}を{察知|さっち}する: to sense danger\n- {異変|いへん}を{察知|さっち}する: to detect something unusual\n- {気配|けはい}を{察知|さっち}する: to sense a presence\n- いち{早|はや}く{察知|さっち}する: to be quick to detect\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {感知|かんち}: detection — more technical, often used for sensors and devices detecting physical phenomena\n- {察|さっ}する: to sense, to surmise — the underlying verb, slightly more literary\n- {気|き}づく: to notice — more colloquial and general, without the implication of intuitive perception",
